    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66">

                <pb facs="0072" n="58" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg58"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.00/1–347: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in France </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-01-08T13:00:00-05:00">January 8, 1947—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>59. Following is text of unnumbered, undated tel from Hanoi received Jan 3:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of telegram 1, January 3, <ref target="#pg53">page
                    53</ref>.]</p>
                <p>Saigon Tel 494, Dec 23,<anchor n="25" xml:id="d66-f1"/> reported official
                    communiqué had quoted Amer, Chinese Consuls Hanoi as characterizing Vietnam
                    action as criminal folly and bestial.</p>
                <p>Dept extremely surprised this attempt local French place US in partisan position.
                    Request you call attention FonOff this matter, taking view, in consideration
                    O’Sullivan’s denial, that correction should be made through Federal Information
                    Service Saigon if such was channel of distribution original communiqué, and
                    through whatever other channels were employed. You may say Consul Saigon
                    expressing same view High Commissioner.<anchor n="26" xml:id="d66-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Saigon be guided by above</p>
                <p>Sent to Paris 59. Repeated Saigon 4.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d66-f1" n="25" xml:id="d66-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d66-f2" n="26" xml:id="d66-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 192, January 16, noon, from Paris, the Embassy reported taking up
                    this matter with the Foreign Office which felt it could best be arranged in
                    Saigon between Admiral d’Atgenlieu and Consul Reed (8510.00/1–1647).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
